Experiment 8 - HMAC integrity and tampering detection
=====================================================
Protocol: edit data/users.json directly, then inspect and try to load it.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+--------+------------------------------------------------+
| Check                                                           | Result | Detail                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+--------+------------------------------------------------+
| changed password hash: baseline file is valid                   | PASS   | json: integrity OK (2 record(s) verified)      |
| changed password hash: offline check detects the change         | PASS   | json: INTEGRITY FAILURE - HMAC digest mismatch |
| changed password hash: load refused (data not trusted)          | PASS   |                                                |
| changed password hash: integrity failure audited                | PASS   | 1 event(s)                                     |
| changed password hash: file not rewritten by failed load        | PASS   |                                                |
| reset failed-attempt counter: baseline file is valid            | PASS   | json: integrity OK (2 record(s) verified)      |
| reset failed-attempt counter: offline check detects the change  | PASS   | json: INTEGRITY FAILURE - HMAC digest mismatch |
| reset failed-attempt counter: load refused (data not trusted)   | PASS   |                                                |
| reset failed-attempt counter: integrity failure audited         | PASS   | 1 event(s)                                     |
| reset failed-attempt counter: file not rewritten by failed load | PASS   |                                                |
| removed lockout: baseline file is valid                         | PASS   | json: integrity OK (2 record(s) verified)      |
| removed lockout: offline check detects the change               | PASS   | json: INTEGRITY FAILURE - HMAC digest mismatch |
| removed lockout: load refused (data not trusted)                | PASS   |                                                |
| removed lockout: integrity failure audited                      | PASS   | 1 event(s)                                     |
| removed lockout: file not rewritten by failed load              | PASS   |                                                |
| deleted user record: baseline file is valid                     | PASS   | json: integrity OK (2 record(s) verified)      |
| deleted user record: offline check detects the change           | PASS   | json: INTEGRITY FAILURE - HMAC digest mismatch |
| deleted user record: load refused (data not trusted)            | PASS   |                                                |
| deleted user record: integrity failure audited                  | PASS   | 1 event(s)                                     |
| deleted user record: file not rewritten by failed load          | PASS   |                                                |
| wrong HMAC key is rejected                                      | PASS   | json: INTEGRITY FAILURE - HMAC digest mismatch |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+--------+------------------------------------------------+

Notes:
  - The HMAC covers the entire user payload, so deleting a record or editing a non-secret field is detected just like a changed hash.
  - Prototype limitation: the key sits next to the data file. An attacker who can read the key can forge the digest; production needs KMS/OS-keyring storage.
  - JSON storage caches records in memory; tampering is detected at load or when verify_integrity() is called. SQLite re-verifies every row on read (Experiment 10).

RESULT: 21/21 checks passed
